 "dependency_review": "Inspected the intake row (notion_id 3b431704-6eeb-81ab-87d1-d7893b35065d, recording 2026-09-21 14-19-53, Notion idea 'Prime Agent release'), the approved plan and handoff, and the title the approved whiteboard generator carries ('Prime Agent: one tool that builds every tool'), which is the package title. The three editable projects each carry index.html; every local src/href resolves inside its tree, and the whiteboard's assets folder is a symlink into stage/primeagent_whiteboard that delivery materializes as real files. Generators: primeagent_scene.py, the split, cutout (plus envelope) and whiteboard generators, the review helpers and _primeagent_proof.py; their imports resolve to pipeline/captions.py, pipeline/pointing_cues.py, formats/cutout/lib (cutout_core, cutout_depthfield) and formats/whiteboard/lib (whiteboard_build, whiteboard_fix6_core), all included; the rest is stdlib, numpy, PIL and playwright. Media and timing: the raw recording, its full Scribe transcript, the whole cuts/primeagent set (master, face plates, audio, EDL, tight transcript) and the prep stage records. Matting: the matting/primeagent session (selection with Astra edits, v5 layers and their pre-fallback copies, plates, cache) and the matting_fallback/primeagent fb1 session the shipped cutout matte came from. Config and paperwork: every gen/_*primeagent* build, cue, envelope, gate, geometry, prerender, pill-width, QC, render-control, spec, whiteboard and word-sync record. Review: final_primeagent.json (Miguel's approval on the staged videos), agent start/done/state records, Astra matte and render logs, page and cutout frame reviews, proof crops, sheets and staging verification. External runtime dependencies recorded, not vendored: GSAP 3.14.2 from jsDelivr and Google Fonts at render time, HyperFrames CLI, Playwright Chromium and ffmpeg. No secrets and no other Short's files."
